# SocratiCode semantic-index exclusions (gitignore syntax).
# Layered on top of SocratiCode's built-in defaults + .gitignore.
#
# Exclude the vendored skill trees. skills-vendor/ holds the git-submodule
# skill repos (~hundreds of files); indexing them inflates embedding time and
# lets vendored skill prose outrank this repo's own code in codebase_search.
# .claude/skills/ holds only symlinks (into skills/), so it carries no real
# content of its own.
# skills/ is deliberately NOT excluded: SocratiCode does not follow symlinks, so
# the vendor symlinks under it index nothing, while the repo's own first-party
# skill overrides (real dirs under skills/, e.g. shipping-work-python-fastapi)
# stay indexed. See GH #160.
skills-vendor/
.claude/skills/
#
# Dated prose leaves the code index so superseded designs stop outranking
# source in codebase_search. All three stay searchable through
# codebase_context_search as directory artifacts (plans, specs, research) —
# the context store is governed by the manifest, not this file. See GH #179.
docs/research/
docs/plans/
docs/specs/
